# `.take` on an `is native` function. A native has no reference form: the
# compiler supplies the body, and an inlined one -- a binop, a conversion --
# has no C function whose address there is to take. Before this was checked,
# zc exited 0 and emitted a CALL typed by a function typedef it never wrote,
# and the build died at `unknown type name 'z_t13_ft'`.
main: function is {
    f: os.cpuCount.take
    print "unreachable"
}
